% formalizes: claim:ethics-a5
% claim: Axiom V: things with nothing in common cannot be understood through each other
% says: Things which have nothing in common cannot be understood, the one by means of the other; the conception of one does not involve the conception of the other.
bottom :- nothing_in_common(X, Y), conception_involves(X, Y).
bottom :- nothing_in_common(X, Y), conception_involves(Y, X).
